      "text": "Regarded by the Jews as of great importance (whereas Egyptians always shaved); the trimming of the corners was forbidden (Lev. 19:26–28), such a practice being a mark of idolatry (Jer. 41:5). See also 1 Sam. 21:13; 2 Sam. 10:4. A leper was compelled to shave (Lev. 14:9).",
